ipation, technical competence. Concerns: not open to new ideas (adaptability), unhealthy eating (maybe reliability). No info on stress resilience, communication. So mixed.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, but makes nasty remarks, sometimes wrong tone. Strengths: reliability, stress resilience, technical (weather, computer). Concerns: professionalism, communication.\n\nCandidate C: makes correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, understands complicated technology, excellent attention. Strengths: decision quality, technical competence, attention. Concerns: communication, teamwork, adaptability.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, has hot temper, regarded as loner. Strengths: problem solving, responsibility, adaptability? Concerns: hot temper, loner (crew cooperation).\n\nWe need to start discussion. Perhaps pick Candidate B as leading due to strong reliability and stress handling, but note communication concerns. Provide vote for B, but open to discussion.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nProceed."}
